      "math_academy_id": "q-93972",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 5+4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =4+15-12 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
